
105 ECOVIEW~
Syntax: ecoview
        ecoview <area name>

Displays detailed economic information for the current area or a specified area.

Shows:
- Production levels for all resources (food, wood, stone, metal, herbs)
- Consumption rates
- Surplus/deficit for each resource  
- Resource prices (buy and sell)
- Area wealth and population
- Economic events affecting the area
- Number of workers by profession

This command helps immortals monitor the health of area economies and identify
imbalances that may need intervention.

See also: ECOSET, ECOBALANCE, ECONEWS, ECONOMY
~

105 ECOSET~
Syntax: ecoset <area> production <resource> <amount>
        ecoset <area> consumption <resource> <amount>
        ecoset <area> price <resource> <buy price> <sell price>
        ecoset <area> wealth <amount>

Manually adjust economic parameters for an area.

Resources: food, wood, stone, metal, herbs

Examples:
  ecoset midgaard production food 500
  ecoset newgate price metal 100 80
  ecoset thalos wealth 50000

Use with caution - the economy auto-balances over time. Manual changes should
only be made to fix severe imbalances or create special economic situations.

See also: ECOVIEW, ECOBALANCE, ECOEVENT
~

105 ECOEVENT~
Syntax: ecoevent <area> <event type>

Trigger an economic event in an area.

Event types:
  drought    - Reduces food production
  plague     - Reduces population and workers
  boom       - Increases all production
  bust       - Decreases area wealth
  bandit     - Random resource losses
  festival   - Temporary wealth increase

Events last for a set duration and automatically resolve. They create dynamic
economic challenges and opportunities for players.

See also: ECOVIEW, ECONEWS
~

105 ECOBALANCE~
Syntax: ecobalance
        ecobalance <area>

Displays auto-balance status for all areas or a specific area.

Shows:
- Areas with severe imbalances
- Resources in deficit
- Suggested interventions
- Auto-balance history (number of interventions)

The economy system automatically balances itself, but this command helps
identify persistent problems that may need immortal attention.

See also: ECOVIEW, ECOSET
~

105 ECONEWS~
Syntax: econews

Displays recent economic news from all regions.

Shows major economic events, market changes, and regional developments.
News items are timestamped and show which region/area was affected.

Useful for tracking economic trends and understanding market dynamics.

See also: ECOVIEW, ECOEVENT
~

0 HARVEST~
Syntax: harvest

Harvest resources from a resource node in your current room.

Resource nodes spawn in specific locations and regenerate over time. Different
areas have different resources available (farms have food, forests have wood,
mines have stone/metal, groves have herbs).

Harvested resources can be sold to merchants or used in crafting.

The amount harvested depends on:
- Your profession (farmers harvest more food, miners more ore, etc.)
- The node's current capacity
- Time since last harvest

See also: PROFESSION, GETWATER, ECONOMY
~

0 GETWATER~
Syntax: getwater

Fill a container with water from a water source in your current room.

Water sources include wells, fountains, rivers, and springs. Some sources
are cleaner than others (springs > wells > fountains > rivers).

Water sources can be depleted if used too heavily, but regenerate over time.

You must have an empty container (waterskin, flask, bottle) to collect water.

See also: HARVEST
~

0 PROFESSION~
Syntax: profession
        profession <profession name>

View your current profession or change to a new one.

Available professions:
  farmer      - Harvests food more efficiently
  miner       - Harvests stone and metal more efficiently
  lumberjack  - Harvests wood more efficiently
  herbalist   - Harvests herbs more efficiently
  merchant    - Better prices when trading
  artisan     - Crafting bonuses (future feature)

Your profession affects:
- Resource harvest rates
- Trade prices with NPCs
- Access to profession-specific abilities

Changing professions has a cooldown period to prevent abuse.

See also: HARVEST, ECONOMY
~

105 OLLAMA~
Syntax: ollama <prompt>

Send a prompt to the Ollama AI system and receive a response.

This is the low-level interface to the AI system. The prompt is sent directly
to the configured Ollama model and the response is displayed.

Examples:
  ollama Describe a mysterious forest clearing
  ollama Generate a backstory for a wandering minstrel

More specialized commands use Ollama internally:
- BEELER ASSIGN - Uses AI to generate NPC personalities
- GENPERSONALITY - Uses AI for mob identity generation
- AI context analysis in various systems

Requires Ollama service to be running and configured in mud.h

See also: BEELER, GENPERSONALITY, MOBIDENTITY
~

105 MOBIDENTITY~
Syntax: mobidentity <mob>
        mobidentity <mob> set <field> <value>
        mobidentity <mob> create

View or modify a mob's identity data.

Identity fields:
  who_am_i       - First person description of self
  what_i_do      - What they do for a living
  how_i_do_it    - Their methods/approach
  where_i_live   - Their home
  where_i_go     - Places they visit
  my_purpose     - Their life goal
  ai_prompt      - AI personality prompt
  schedule       - Daily schedule (sleep/work/free times)

Examples:
  mobidentity baker
  mobidentity baker set who_am_i I am a skilled baker
  mobidentity 1234 create

The identity system gives NPCs personality, goals, and context-aware behavior.
Combined with the AI system, mobs can have realistic conversations and
remember interactions with players.

See also: GENPERSONALITY, MOBMEMORY, BEELER ASSIGN
~

105 GENPERSONALITY~
Syntax: genpersonality <mob>

Generate an AI-powered personality for a mob.

This command analyzes the mob's description, location, and context, then uses
AI to generate appropriate identity fields and personality traits.

The generated identity includes:
- Who/what/how/where/why (identity fields)
- Personality traits
- Daily schedule
- AI conversation prompt

This is a quick way to give a mob personality without manually setting all
fields. For more control, use BEELER ASSIGN which also considers economic
context and assigns professions.

See also: MOBIDENTITY, BEELER ASSIGN, OLLAMA
~

105 MOBMEMORY~
Syntax: mobmemory <mob>

Display a mob's memory of past interactions.

Shows:
- Encounters with players
- Significant events
- Emotional responses
- Remembered conversations

Mobs with high awareness levels remember more details and for longer periods.
This memory influences their behavior and dialogue with returning players.

The memory system makes NPCs feel more alive and responsive to player actions.

See also: MOBIDENTITY, BEELER ASSIGN
~

105 ECONOMY~
The Economic Ecosystem System

cosMUD features a comprehensive dynamic economy system where:

Area Economics:
- Each area produces and consumes resources (food, wood, stone, metal, herbs)
- Areas trade with each other based on supply and demand
- Prices fluctuate based on availability
- Economic events (droughts, booms, etc.) affect production

NPC Professions:
- NPCs have professions that determine what they produce
- Farmers grow food, miners extract ore, lumberjacks harvest wood
- The system auto-balances professions based on area needs

Player Interaction:
- Players can harvest resources from nodes
- Collect water from wells and springs
- Trade with NPC merchants at dynamic prices
- Choose professions that affect harvest rates

Auto-Balancing:
- The economy adjusts itself to fix imbalances
- Areas in deficit attract more workers in needed professions
- Prices rise when resources are scarce
- The system logs interventions for monitoring

Commands: ECOVIEW, ECOSET, ECOEVENT, ECOBALANCE, ECONEWS, HARVEST, 
          GETWATER, PROFESSION

Related Systems: MOB IDENTITY, BEELER

The economy creates a living world where player actions have meaningful impact.
~

